  "decision": "Retain the historical distinctUntilChanged comparison of both completion state names. The untouched complete historical base and actual owned base produce equal outputs for duplicate center/leave, repeat real cycles, changed source/destination, obsolete states and origin-center names. Removing the filter changes the reference contract. Both exact current minimum peer completion methods emit twice on synthetic duplicate calls and use current MDC/native motion; they do not own or qualify the add-on legacy subscription. Original group template routes _onCentered to _removeTabBodyWrapperHeight, which emits public animationDone; portal detach receives _afterLeavingCenter. Preserve this contract rather than falsely claiming the newer removal was ported.",
  "repairs": [
    "Replace fabricated tab notification count0 with the actual public animationDone subscription; dispatch two duplicate native end events and retain its measured count.",
    "Require tab completion for enabled/provider-disabled/reduced/zero contexts across three engines and two runtimes; remove the false no-public-completion exception.",
    "Bind each branch generator/validator/matrix/coordinator to its own source line; reject foreign namespace IDs and inspect actual branch consumer version selection."
  ],
